#X text 1080 205 OSC OUT -- the OLED graphics API. This shows WHAT is drawn \, not WHERE. Positioned rendering is deliberately out of scope., f 40;
#X obj 1080 300 u_oled-preview;
#X text 1080 340 shows what the patch draws \, one box per screen line. Its own file because it grew past what belongs in a shim -- and because Phase 3 will lean on it hard., f 40;
#X text 1080 440 The self-test buttons moved INTO u_oled-preview \, next to the boxes they affect. Pressing in one window and watching another was unusable., f 58;
#X text 1080 930 gPrintln: drop the typetag \, then screen \, x \, y \, height and colour -- what is left is the text. gClear blanks the box. gFlip and gShowInfoBar are ignored on purpose: they would flood the console., f 58;
#X text 20 890 AUDIO -- mirrors mother.pd's audioIO subpatch \, so that "it sounds right on the Mac" means something. mother publishes the inputs on inL / inR and collects the output from outL / outR. Nothing makes a sound until DSP is on AND a generator is picked -- both are off at load \, on purpose., f 58;
#X obj 640 1000 tgl 15 0 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X msg 700 1000 \; pd dsp \$1;
#X text 830 1000 DSP -- off at load;
#X text 20 1035 inL: silence / tone 220 / noise, f 34;
#X obj 20 1065 hradio 15 1 0 3 empty empty empty 0 -8 0 10 -262144 -1 -1 0;
#X obj 20 1100 t f f;
#X obj 180 1140 == 1;
#X obj 410 1140 == 2;
#X obj 20 1175 osc~ 220;
#X obj 250 1175 noise~;
#X obj 100 1215 *~ 0;
#X obj 330 1215 *~ 0;
#X obj 100 1255 *~ 0.2;
#X obj 100 1290 s~ inL;
#X text 520 1035 inR: silence / tone 330 / noise, f 34;
#X obj 520 1065 hradio 15 1 0 3 empty empty empty 0 -8 0 10 -262144 -1 -1 0;
#X obj 520 1100 t f f;
#X obj 680 1140 == 1;
#X obj 910 1140 == 2;
#X obj 520 1175 osc~ 330;
#X obj 750 1175 noise~;
#X obj 600 1215 *~ 0;
#X obj 830 1215 *~ 0;
#X obj 600 1255 *~ 0.2;
#X obj 600 1290 s~ inR;
#X text 1020 1100 OUTPUT -- catch what the patch throws \, apply the volume knob the way mother does \, limit \, and play it., f 40;
#X obj 1020 1170 catch~ outL;
#X obj 1180 1170 catch~ outR;
#X obj 1370 1065 r vol;
#X obj 1370 1100 t f f;
#X obj 1370 1135 *;
#X obj 1370 1170 sig~;
#X obj 1370 1215 lop~ 5;
#X obj 1020 1260 *~;
#X obj 1180 1260 *~;
#X obj 1020 1300 clip~ -1 1;
#X obj 1180 1300 clip~ -1 1;
#X obj 1020 1340 dac~;
#X text 1450 1250 vol is a SQUARE law with 5 Hz smoothing \, exactly as mother.pd does it. Without the smoothing the knob zippers., f 30;
#X text 20 1400 THIS SECTION IS WHY THE STUB MUST NEVER LOAD ON THE DEVICE. s~ inL and catch~ outL/outR are names mother.pd already defines \, so a second definition is not a duplicate value -- it is a load error. Two different tone frequencies so the channels are distinguishable by ear as well as by number. No adc~: one laptop mic cannot test a two-channel split \, and it would feed back., f 46;
